From: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
Date: Wed, 14 May 2026
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: widen PPPQ coverage and enable it by default

mtk_ppe_check_pppq_path() was originally written for 5-port mt7530-class
DSA fabrics and direct-GMAC-only boxes, and silently dropped PPPQ in two
configurations we ship:

  1. Non-DSA direct GMAC ports (dsa_port < 0) were rejected outright, so
     PPE-offloaded flows on those boxes never got a QDMA queue assignment.
     Without one, the PPE pushes packets at SerDes rate regardless of
     actual link speed, hurting throughput when routing between mismatched
     speeds.

  2. DSA user-port indices > 4 (with a special-case for index 5 only on
     wifi-ingress flows) were rejected, so on larger DSA fabrics like the
     MXL86282 the higher-numbered user ports never received a per-port
     queue. PPE-offloaded flows for those ports landed on the FOE-default
     QID 0 and showed up on the conduit's base queue instead of the
     per-port queue. mac->dsa_user_idx[] is already sized for 16 entries,
     so the storage side is fine; only the gate was lagging.

Relax the gate: any DSA user port whose index fits in mac->dsa_user_idx[],
and any non-DSA direct GMAC, now goes through PPPQ.

Also default eth->qos_toggle to 2 (PPPQ mode) at probe time. The field
is u8 and zero-initialised by devm_kzalloc(), so today PPE-offloaded
flows skip the queue-assignment branch entirely unless something in
userspace writes "2" to the debugfs qos_toggle node. Defaulting to 2
finishes the rate-limiting story for our SKUs.

Tested on MT7987A with 3 direct GMACs (no DSA switch):
  Routed NAT, 1G LAN (2500base-x) <-> 2.5G WAN, HW offload + PPPQ
  Before: 662 Mbps downstream
  After:  941 Mbps downstream

Signed-off-by: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c |    7 +++++++
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h |   12 +++++++++---
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
@@ -1789,10 +1789,16 @@ static inline u32 mtk_get_ib2_multicast_
 static inline int
 mtk_ppe_check_pppq_path(struct mtk_mac *mac, struct net_device *idev, int dsa_port)
 {
-	bool wifi_rx = !!(idev->ieee80211_ptr);
+	/* DSA user ports - any index that fits the per-port idx table.
+	 * The old "<= 4" cap (with a port-5/wifi_rx quirk) was sized for
+	 * mt7530-class 5-port switches and silently dropped PPPQ on
+	 * larger DSA fabrics.
+	 */
+	if (dsa_port >= 0 && dsa_port < ARRAY_SIZE(mac->dsa_user_idx))
+		return 1;
 
-	if ((dsa_port >= 0 && dsa_port <= 4) ||
-	    (dsa_port == 5 && wifi_rx))
+	/* Non-DSA direct GMAC ports */
+	if (dsa_port < 0)
 		return 1;
 
 	return 0;
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -6340,6 +6340,12 @@ static int mtk_probe(struct platform_dev
 
 	eth->soc = of_device_get_match_data(&pdev->dev);
 
+	/* Default to per-port-per-queue (PPPQ) mode so PPE flows pick up
+	 * the per-egress-port QDMA queue assignment that rate-limits at
+	 * the actual link speed.
+	 */
+	eth->qos_toggle = 2;
+
 	eth->dev = &pdev->dev;
 	eth->dma_dev = &pdev->dev;
 	eth->base = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
